    {
      "id": "vkpye6x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Time Period of the Vedic Age"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Vedic Period is broadly divided into the Early Vedic Period (1500–1000 BCE) and the Later Vedic Period (1000–500 BCE).",
        "The literary corpus comprises the four Vedas: Rigveda, Samaveda, Yajurveda, and Atharvaveda.",
        "Political power transitioned from tribal chieftainships (Rajan) supported by tribal assemblies to territorial kingdoms (Janapadas).",
        "Democratic tribal assemblies such as Sabha, Samiti, and Vidatha played a significant role in governance during the Early Vedic era.",
        "The economy shifted from a predominantly pastoral and nomadic lifestyle to settled agriculture assisted by the discovery of iron."
      ],
      "id": "b4qbw4y"
    },
